│   ✅ Agent Finished                                                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│   Message:                                                                                                                                     │
│     The fix is in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py`: `get_parameterless_sub_dependant`, which builds the dependency entries for                  │
│ `dependencies=[...]` at app, router and route level, never attached a `SecurityRequirement` for security-scheme dependencies, so they were     │
│ dropped from the OpenAPI output. It now attaches the requirement the same way `get_dependant` does.                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     I confirmed the fix with a small app: before the change `app.openapi()` had no `components` at all, and after it both schemes appear with  │
│ the correct `security` entries. I ran `tests/test_security_api_key_header.py` and `tests/test_dependency_cache.py` (7 passed). I did not write │
│ a dedicated regression test, and I did not run the wider OpenAPI or security test files.                                                       │
